      "label": "Teal-colored foliage",
      "description": "Distinctive blue-green to emerald coloration of leaves that intensifies in cooler months",
      "isPrimary": true
    },
    {
      "label": "Pin-like structures",
      "description": "Thin, needle-like reproductive appendages that extend from branch terminals",
      "isPrimary": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Compact growth form",
      "description": "Dense, shrubby habit typically reaching 2-4 feet in height with fine, feathery branching",
      "isPrimary": false
    }
  ],
  "habitat": "This species thrives in well-drained, acidic soils of mixed woodland understories and shaded garden settings throughout New England.",
